OL,3,ABurnham 'open' to calls for slavery
OL,4,Aapology but not reparations
OL,5,
OL,6,FPrime Minister Andy Burnham says he is
OL,7,F"open" to the possibility of the UK
OL,8,Fformally apologising for its role in
OL,9,Fthe transatlantic slave trade, but has
OL,10,Fruled out financial reparations.
OL,12,FHe said he wanted a "dialogue with
OL,13,Fthose affected" and was open to "calls
OL,14,Ffor an apology", but said reparations
OL,15,Fwere "not the right answer".
OL,17,FThe statement was welcomed by the
OL,18,FAll-Party Parliamentary Group (APPG)
OL,19,Ffor Afrikan Reparations, with its chair
OL,20,FBell Ribeiro-Adday telling BBC Radio
OL,21,F4's Today programme the issue was not
OL,22,Fjust about money.
OL,23,APub: 31-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
